   "source": [
    "# COX-2 model training\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells top to bottom. Only **cell 1** needs editing.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What changed:** the raw table now carries the descriptor columns already, so\n",
    "nothing is featurised during training. Features are read straight from the\n",
    "table. SMILES are only needed for the similarity checks and for scoring new\n",
    "molecules; the notebook detects whether they are present and skips what it cannot do.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime:** roughly 30-50 minutes with the default settings. The GPU is not\n",
    "used; scikit-learn random forests run on CPU. More cores means faster.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Needs:** `rdkit scikit-learn optuna shap joblib pandas numpy matplotlib scipy`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ff22c9db",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Settings — edit this cell"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8d24f841",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Column names in the raw CSV. None = detect automatically.\n",
    "LABEL_COL = None   # e.g. \"Activity\"\n",
    "SMILES_COL = None  # e.g. \"Smiles\"; fine to leave as None if there is none\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop rows whose feature vectors are identical. The descriptors are\n",
    "# stereo-blind, so stereoisomers become duplicate rows; where they disagree\n",
    "# about the label the model cannot resolve them and they leak across splits.\n",
    "DEDUPE = True\n",
    "\n",
    "# How long the hyperparameter search may run, PER split mode.\n",
    "# Stops at whichever limit is reached first. \"both\" runs it twice.\n",
    "N_TRIALS = 30\n",
    "TIMEOUT_MIN = 45\n",
    "\n",
    "# \"both\" = random + scaffold (recommended: the gap is a result in itself)\n",
    "SPLIT_MODE = \"both\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Explainability\n",
    "TARGET_CLASS = 1          # class to explain, 1 = active\n",
    "ONLY_IN_DOMAIN = True    # explain only test molecules similar to the training data\n",
    "SHAP_MAX_MOLECULES = 500  # TreeSHAP on a large forest is slow, so subsample"
   ]
  },
